                <pb facs="0746" n="636" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg636"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/3091: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-12-08T10:00:00+08:00">December 8, 1931—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 8—12:43 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1052. A member of the Military Attaché’s office yesterday was shown a telegram to
                    Marshal Chang Hsueh-liang from T. V. Soong stating that the negotiations for a
                    neutral zone were likely to fail and that any Japanese attack on Chinchow should
                    be offered utmost resistance.</p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
